  {
    "description": "List the durable facts remembered about the user — use it to answer "what do you remember about me", and to get a fact's id before correcting or retracting it. Every line starts with the fact's id ("- id <uuid>: ..."): copy that id VERBATIM into manage_fact's factId — never invent or abbreviate it. Each fact is listed grouped by category, with its durability class, confirmation count and last-updated date. Set includeArchived=true only when the user asks what used to be remembered: archived facts come with their closure reason.",
    "name": "list_facts",
    "schema": {
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "includeArchived": {
          "description": "Include archived (closed) facts with their closure reason.",
          "type": "boolean",
        },
      },
      "type": "object",
    },
  },
]
`;

exports[`tool surface (pre-executor truth, refactor-p3-tool-executor Task 1) registration tool surface 1`] = `
[
  {
    "description": "Save one or more profile fields the user has provided. Extract and save age, gender, height (cm), weight (kg), fitness level, or goal from what the user said. Only include fields explicitly mentioned in this message. Can be called multiple times as the user provides info across the conversation.",
    "name": "save_profile_fields",
    "schema": {
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "age": {
          "description": "Age in years (10–120)",
          "type": "number",
        },
        "firstName": {
          "description": "Preferred name if user provides one",
          "type": "string",
        },
        "fitnessGoal": {
          "description": "Fitness goal in their own words",
          "type": "string",
        },
        "fitnessLevel": {
          "description": "Self-assessed fitness level",
          "enum": [
            "beginner",
            "intermediate",
            "advanced",
          ],
          "type": "string",
        },
        "gender": {
          "description": "Biological gender",
          "enum": [
            "male",
            "female",
          ],
          "type": "string",
        },
        "height": {
          "description": "Height in cm (100–250)",
          "type": "number",
        },
        "weight": {
          "description": "Weight in kg (20–300)",
          "type": "number",
        },
      },
      "type": "object",
    },
  },
  {
    "description": "Mark registration as complete and transition the user to the next phase. Call this ONLY when all 6 profile fields are collected AND the user has explicitly confirmed the summary. The user must say something like "yes", "correct", "looks good", "ok", etc. Pass toPhase="plan_creation" if user wants to start training, "chat" if they want to ask questions first.",
    "name": "complete_registration",
    "schema": {
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "toPhase": {
          "description": "Next phase: "plan_creation" if user wants to build a plan, "chat" if they want to talk first",
          "enum": [
            "plan_creation",
            "chat",
          ],
          "type": "string",
        },
      },
      "required": [
        "toPhase",
      ],
      "type": "object",
    },
  },
  {
    "description": "Save the user's timezone. Call when the user provides their city or timezone. Use IANA format, e.g. "Europe/Berlin", "America/New_York", "Asia/Tokyo".",
    "name": "save_timezone",
    "schema": {
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "timezone": {
          "description": "IANA timezone string, e.g. "Europe/Berlin"",
          "type": "string",
        },
      },
      "required": [
        "timezone",
      ],
      "type": "object",
    },
  },
  {
    "description": "Manage the durable facts you remember about the user. operation "save": store a fact the user just stated, or CORRECT an existing one (same meaning, new details — pass the corrected text). Pick durability by what the user described: "permanent" only for irreversible conditions (say so only when the user stated it explicitly — otherwise the call is rejected); "long_term" for injuries/recoveries measured in weeks or months (pass reviewInDays and a short phaseNote); "short" for states that resolve in days (pass ttlDays and on_expiry: "forget" for things that certainly pass like soreness or bad sleep, "ask_once" for a tweak or pain under load that may leave a trace). operation "retract": the user says a fact is no longer true or applies ("that is fine now", "stop using that") — the fact is ARCHIVED: kept in history, never used or asked about again. operation "delete": the user explicitly does not want a fact STORED at all ("erase that", privacy) — the fact is removed entirely, no trace. For retract/delete, identify the fact EITHER by factId (copied verbatim from a list_facts line, which starts with "- id <uuid>:") OR by factQuery — the distinctive words of what the user called it (e.g. "lower back"); if several facts match the query you will get their ids back — re-call with the right one. Never tell the user a fact was removed unless the tool call succeeded. retract and delete are DIFFERENT operations: if it is unclear which the user means, DO NOT call the tool — ask them first ("should I stop using this fact, or erase it completely?"). For delete, set confirmed=true ONLY after the user explicitly confirmed permanent erasure.",
    "name": "manage_fact",
    "schema": {
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "category": {
          "description": "For save: the fact category.",
          "enum": [
            "physical_constraint",
            "exercise_preference",
            "exercise_dislike",
            "physiological_pattern",
            "coaching_preference",
            "schedule_constraint",
            "equipment",
            "nutrition_preference",
          ],
          "type": "string",
        },
        "confirmed": {
          "description": "For delete: true ONLY after the user explicitly confirmed permanent erasure.",
          "type": "boolean",
        },
        "context": {
          "description": "For save: a short "how we learned this".",
          "type": "string",
        },
        "durability": {
          "description": "For save: how long the fact holds (see the tool description for how to choose).",
          "enum": [
            "permanent",
            "long_term",
            "short",
          ],
          "type": "string",
        },
        "explicitPermanent": {
          "description": "For save + permanent: true when the user explicitly stated irreversibility.",
          "type": "boolean",
        },
        "fact": {
          "description": "For save: the fact in one clear sentence.",
          "minLength": 3,
          "type": "string",
        },
        "factId": {
          "description": "For retract/delete, and for save when CORRECTING an existing fact: the fact id, verbatim from list_facts.",
          "format": "uuid",
          "pattern": "^([0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[1-8][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[89abAB][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12}|00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000|ffffffff-ffff-ffff-ffff-ffffffffffff)$",
          "type": "string",
        },
        "factQuery": {
          "description": "For retract/delete without a factId: what the user called the fact, in its own distinctive words (e.g. "lower back").",
          "minLength": 3,
          "type": "string",
        },
        "muscleGroup": {
          "description": "For save: the muscle group, when the fact is anatomical.",
          "type": "string",
        },
        "onExpiry": {
          "description": "For save + short: what happens on expiry.",
          "enum": [
            "forget",
            "ask_once",
          ],
          "type": "string",
        },
        "operation": {
          "description": "What to do with the fact.",
          "enum": [
            "save",
            "retract",
            "delete",
          ],
          "type": "string",
        },
        "phaseNote": {
          "description": "For save + long_term: the recovery phase in the user’s words.",
          "type": "string",
        },
        "reviewInDays": {
          "description": "For save + long_term: days until you should re-ask about it (14–182).",
          "exclusiveMinimum": 0,
          "maximum": 9007199254740991,
          "type": "integer",
        },
        "supersedesFactId": {
          "description": "For save: id of the CLOSED fact this statement replaces (from list_facts).",
          "format": "uuid",
          "pattern": "^([0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[1-8][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[89abAB][0-9a-fA-F]{3}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12}|00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000|ffffffff-ffff-ffff-ffff-ffffffffffff)$",
          "type": "string",
        },
        "ttlDays": {
          "description": "For save + short: days until it expires (1–14).",
          "exclusiveMinimum": 0,
          "maximum": 9007199254740991,
          "type": "integer",
        },
      },
      "required": [
        "operation",
      ],
      "type": "object",
    },
  },
  {
    "description": "List the durable facts remembered about the user — use it to answer "what do you remember about me", and to get a fact's id before correcting or retracting it. Every line starts with the fact's id ("- id <uuid>: ..."): copy that id VERBATIM into manage_fact's factId — never invent or abbreviate it. Each fact is listed grouped by category, with its durability class, confirmation count and last-updated date. Set includeArchived=true only when the user asks what used to be remembered: archived facts come with their closure reason.",
    "name": "list_facts",
    "schema": {
      "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "includeArchived": {
          "description": "Include archived (closed) facts with their closure reason.",
          "type": "boolean",
        },
      },
      "type": "object",
    },
  },
]
